# Durable memory for this repo

Memory lives in the Systems folder in Dropbox. Its path is the SYSTEMS_ROOT value in `~/.config/data-roots.env` (read that file; never guess the path, and never use the old `~/ObsidianVault`, which no longer exists).

Before your first substantive response in a session here, read both of these straight from disk, under that folder:

1. `memory/global/MEMORY.md`
2. `memory/atomic-agents-stack/MEMORY.md`

`atomic-agents-stack` is this repo's memory folder. It is stated here so you do not have to look it up. If `memory/memory-map.md` disagrees with it, that file wins and you should say so.

Both are indexes, one line per memory. **Open an individual note only when its line looks relevant to the task.** Do not read the whole folder.

These files hold corrections already given and decisions already made. Reading them is how you avoid repeating a conversation that already happened.

**Memory is read-only.** Never create, edit, delete, move, or reorganize anything in the Systems folder. When something is worth remembering, say so and hand over the note text instead of saving it.

If `~/.config/data-roots.env` is missing or the folder can't be read, say so once and work without memory. Never invent what a memory says.
